  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\n   - **Central idea**: We use constraint-aware surrogate representation with geometric optimization and multi-resolution ensemble learning to escape local optima. Our approach combines a low-dimensional latent space representation with physics-informed priors to capture optimal overlap reduction patterns, then trains a multi-resolution ascent model to extrapolate promising solutions beyond 0.38085 thresholds.\n   - **Bottleneck**: Non-convex optimization has not yet escaped the 0.38085 bound despite prior attempts. This approach better handles geometric nonlinearities by:\n     - Projecting solutions into a conservative reduced space ($S^{n-1}$ intersected with $\u2211h_i \\geq$ cases)\n     - Using Chebyshev surrogate models to capture extremal correlation patterns\n     - Implementing resolution-invariant transition operators for cross-grid optimization\n   - **Limitations**: Requires theoretical justification for convexity preservation; validation relies entirely on provided eval_erdos_solution.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\n   - **Representation**: \n     - Base grid: $n$, $dx=2/n$\n     - Latent variables: Solution gradients at top-10 lags encoded via Dirac features $\\delta_{k}$ (Kullback-Leibler divergence bounded)\n     - Objective: Minimize $C\u2085 = \\max_k \\frac{2}{n} \\sum_i \\sum_j h_i (1-h_j) \\delta_{i-j=k}$\n   - **Constraints**:\n     - $\u2200i: 0 \\leq h_i \\leq 1$ enforced via projection\n     - $\u2211_i h_i = n/2$ enforced explicitly in all stages\n   - **Surrogate formulation**:\n     - Chebyshev approximants trained over $L^\\infty$-balls of admissible functions\n     - Coefficients weighted by aggregation stability $\\gamma_k = \\min_{1\\leq m \\leq n} |\\frac{\\partial C\u2085}{\\partial h_m}|$\n   - **Resolution handling**:\n     - Generic solution reconstruction via inverse Chebyshev transform\n     - Cross-resolution consistency enforced via transfer operators: $T^{(n')}_{n}(h) = h \u2297 \\phi_{n'/n}$\n\n3. Implementation procedure\n   - **Phase 1: Initial assessment**\n     - Compute parent grid objective $C\u209a$ using provided parent\n     - Identify critical lags $K\u2082\u2080$ (most contributing to max correlation)\n     - Fit polynomial chaos expansion to parent's gradient field\n   \n   - **Phase 2: Geometric optimization**\n     - Employ CG-based method over SR1 updates using top-20 correlation gradients\n     - Parameters: $\\beta_min=7\u2083$, $\\alpha_{max}=0.\u2083$\n     - Line searches: Interpolate cubic descent along projected feasible directions\n\n   - **Phase 3: Surrogate-enhanced exploration**\n     - Train multi-resolution Chebyshev network:\n       - Basis: Altered Legendre basis with perturbation kernel\n       - Regularization: Total variation $\\|h\\|_{TV} \\leq \u03b3$\n       - For reconstruction at resolution $m$, enforce $h^{(m)} \\in$ feasible set\n     - Perform multi-start optimization with $M=12$ initializations:\n       - Sample external space $G \\sim \ud835\udc81(0,0.01)$ from trusted regions\n       - Injective embedding: $\ud835\udd4a^m \\hookrightarrow h + \u03c4 \\cdot G$\n\n   - **Phase 4: Progressive refinement**\n     - Execute Nelder-Mead over top-$K\u2083\u2080$ correlation lags at each resolution\n     - Refine via nested eigenvector continuation when max correlation decrease < $10^{-6}$\n     - Termination criteria:\n       - Relative improvement < $10^{-8}$\n       - Budget $\\approx 1300$ seconds\n\n4. Search choices\n   - **Default runs**:\n     - Main resolution $n_{ref}=1024$\n     - Cleaned latents: Use point-subsets $K\u2083\u2080$ with $\u03c9_k \\geq \\beta^{-1} \\log n$\n     - Surrogate fidelity: Truncate polynomials at degree $\\floor{\\log_2 n}$\n\n   - **Parameters swept**:\n     - TV penalty: $\u03b3=2.5 (1 + \\zeta \\cdot 13.7)$\n     - Max lag samples: $K_{max}=\\{10,15,20,25\\}$\n     - Projection tolerance: $\\epsilon_{clip}=10^{-7}, 5\\cdot10^{-7}, 10^{-6}$\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\n   - **Estimates**:\n     |n|  |Est. time|\n     |---|---------|\n     |256|     10s  |\n     |512|     35s  |\n     |1024|  130s   |\n     |2048|  350s   |\n\n   - **Schedule**:\n     1. n=256: Initial assessment (\u2264120s)\n     2. n=512: Base optimization (\u2264500s)\n     3. n=1024: Final polishing (\u2264700s)\n\n   - **Fallback**:\n     If main path fails, return `$parent_h`, `$parent_c5`, but mark as candidate\n     Recovery step: Run gradient-based polishing at n=512 for 10 minutes\n\n6. Validation and return contract\n   - **Final checks**:\n     1. Bounds: $\u2200i: \\max(h)=1,\\ \\min(h)=0$\n     2. Mass: $|\\sum h - n/2| \\leq 1$\n     3. Objective: $C\u2085 = \\text{compute_c5}(h)$\n\n   - **External validation**:\n     - Call `evaluate_erdos_solution` if $C\u2085 < 0.38081 + 10^{-6}$\n\n   - **Output**:\n     - h_values: Array of candidate solution\n     - c5_bound: Computed constant\n     - n_points: Used resolution (default 1024)",
